  "order": 48,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "57aiutl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Budget"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Under Article 112 of the Constitution of India, the budget is officially termed as the 'Annual Financial Statement'.",
        "The Union Budget is broadly divided into two main components: Revenue Budget and Capital Budget.",
        "Revenue Receipts are non-redeemable receipts that neither create a liability nor cause a reduction in government assets.",
        "Capital Receipts either create a financial liability (e.g., market borrowings) or reduce financial assets (e.g., recovery of loans, disinvestment).",
        "Goods and Services Tax (GST) is a comprehensive multi-stage destination-based tax that subsumed major central and state indirect taxes."
      ],
      "id": "wxfl2j5"
    },
